From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] print tune: Z offset arrows follow the nozzle on the AD5X

On printers whose bed moves in Z, Print Tuning's Z offset buttons show
the bed's direction: closer (the bottom button) has an up arrow, farther
(the top one) a down arrow. The panel draws a nozzle over a scale with
+ at the top, so on the AD5X the nozzle came closer from the button
pointing up. On HELIX_KILN_AD5X builds the arrows follow the nozzle:
farther points up, closer points down. The buttons and what they send
are unchanged.
---
diff --git a/src/ui/ui_print_tune_overlay.cpp b/src/ui/ui_print_tune_overlay.cpp
index 4ce4e74..f1f57ea 100644
--- a/src/ui/ui_print_tune_overlay.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/ui_print_tune_overlay.cpp
@@ -289,6 +289,12 @@ void PrintTuneOverlay::update_z_offset_icons(lv_obj_t* /*panel*/) {
     int kin =
         lv_subject_get_int(printer_state_->capabilities_state().subject(Capability::BedMoves));
     bool bed_moves_z = (kin == 1);
+#if defined(HELIX_KILN_AD5X)
+    // Kiln OS (AD5X): the panel shows a nozzle over a scale with + at the
+    // top, and the buttons say closer and farther, so the arrows follow the
+    // nozzle (down = closer) although the AD5X's bed is what moves.
+    bed_moves_z = false;
+#endif
 
     // Set icon names via string subjects (bind_icon in XML)
     // Closer = more squish. On bed-moves-Z (CoreXY): bed rises (expand_up).
